  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Coastal Gulf of Alaska Bio-physical Model Output (PMEL Ferret FOCI LAS)",
  "description": "A set of nested, three-dimensional circulation model output of the coastal Gulf of Alaska at 3 km resolution. ROMS was implemented tracking the FATE mooring. Dataset variables include dissolved iron, nitrate, phytoplankton, salinity, temperature, vector velocity, velocity-east, and velocity-north, velocity-up. Model output can be viewed via the PMEL Ferret FOCI LAS at http://ferret.pmel.noaa.gov/FOCI/servlets/dataset. FOCI - Fisheries-Oceanography Coordinated Investigations LAS - Liver Access Server PMEL - Pacific Marine Environmental Laboratory ROM - Regional Ocean Modeling System\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To investigate residence time over Portlock Bank near Kodiak, Alaska.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23606272",
